From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devon Openheim <devopenm@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 31 Aug 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] net: wireless: rtl8xxxu: add PCIe bus support for RTL8192FR

Add PCIe transport layer to rtl8xxxu driver to support RTL8192FR
(10ec:818c) and RTL8812FR (10ec:f812) in the Notion R291 for
2.4GHz and 5GHz WiFi respectively.

Key changes to existing code:
- Add struct device *dev and bus_ops to rtl8xxxu_priv for bus-agnostic
  register access
- Replace &priv->udev->dev with priv->dev for logging (bus-agnostic)
- Make mac80211 callbacks non-static and export for PCIe reuse
- Register access functions (read8/16/32, write8/16/32) dispatch through
  bus_ops when set, falling back to USB control messages

New files:
- rtl8xxxu_pcie.c: PCIe transport (MMIO bus_ops, DMA rings, NAPI RX,
  MSI interrupt, PCI probe/remove, mac80211 ops for tx/start/stop)
- rtl8xxxu_pcie.h: PCIe ring descriptors and MMIO register definitions

Signed-off-by: Devon Openheim <devopenm@proton.me>
---

